A change to the thread whose turn a core has, or that pays for it, as a bind to units of another core, does not tell that core,
which neither looks at its run queue again nor, if it is another, is interrupted for it.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a turn its own units give time runs no request on them
Report: a turn on spare time runs while a thread with time waits
Witness: fuzz bind-turn-later

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -494,11 +494,6 @@ static void thread_settle(struct thread *t)
         LOOP_BOUND(CORES);
         place_settle(thread_place(t, i));
     }
-    /* What the turn runs on, and the request it runs, may have changed, so its core looks at its run queue again. */
-    if (is_turn(t)) {
-        cores[t->core].run_stale = true;
-        core_notify(&cores[t->core]);
-    }
 }
 
